840 0 obj
  << /ActualText (About me\nUX\057UI Designer with a background in Visual Communication\056 \nExpert in characterizing and designing B2B products\054 complex systems\054 and consumer apps end\055to\055end\054 from user research to final UI\056 Possesses expertise in building design systems on a semantic token layer\054 leveraging AI tools across the design workflow\054 and grounding design decisions in quantitative and qualitative research\056\n\nExperience\nUX\057UI Designer \174 Freelance   \0502023 \055 2026\051\nLed end\055to\055end \050E2E\051 characterization and design processes for responsive websites\054 portals\054 dashboards\054 and complex systems for a variety of clients\056\nManaged direct workflows with developers \050Hand\055off\051\054 product managers\054 and organizational stakeholders\054 while maintaining business goals and an intuitive user experience\056\nConducted user research\054 built personas\054 information architecture\054 wireframes\054 and complex prototypes to identify and solve pain points in digital work environments\056\nOptimized conversion rates \050CRO\051\054 refined user flows\054 and simplified digital forms to reduce friction\056\n\nProjects\nBianca \174 B2B Restaurant Management Dashboard   \0502026\051\nLed the full design cycle of a B2B system\072 a survey of 48 managers and 572 employees\054 competitor analysis\054 prototyping\054 and a scalable Design System\056\nDesigned a dashboard around decisions\054 not data display\054 cutting the cognitive load found in research\056\nTalmind \174 AI Learning App \046 Design System  \0502025\051\nDesigned an E2E tablet learning app and trained an AI agent that adapts each lesson to its grade level\056\nBuilt its Design System from 72 base tokens\072 a semantic layer over primitives and hand\055off docs for 15 components\056\n\nEDUCATION\nOpen University of Israel   \0502020 \055 2023\051\nB\056A\056 in Visual Communication\n\nProg College   \0502024\051\nUX\057UI Design)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 841 0 R
     /Pg 836 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

